    "result_text": "All tests pass (22 tests, BUILD SUCCESS), including the new `Cp13Tests.coreCountsNamesakes`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, compared case-insensitively.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount.java`: reads the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners in the repository whose firstName and lastName match case-insensitively (via `equalsIgnoreCase`), and stores the count on the owner. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count reflects owners existing before this create and excludes the new owner.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted `assignNamesakeCount` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save` in `owners.POST.yml`.\n\n3. **Domain model** \u2014 added the `Integer namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter to `Owner`. It's a persisted snapshot, so GET returns the value captured at create time.\n\n4. **API schema** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct mapper pick it up automatically by name.\n\n5. **Database schemas** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) and appended the extra `NULL` to the positional owner seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the other data files use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nI used `Integer` (nullable) so pre-existing seed owners with a `NULL` column map cleanly without a Hibernate primitive-null failure.",
